// ADR 0125 §1.1/§1.5/§1.6 end-to-end console coverage (BT-3576): attaches
// to a *real*, `beamtalk release`-assembled node with `[release] console =
// true`, booted from its own generated `.rel`/`start.boot`/`sys.config` —
// the actual `beamtalk_workspace_app:start/2` app-env-driven start path and
// `.app` module activation a deployed release goes through
// (`ProcessManager::start_real_release`) — unlike
// `release_console_default.btscript` / `release_console_include_compiler.btscript`
// (BT-3575), which assert the same wire-level behaviour against a
// hand-started `beamtalk_workspace_sup:start_link/1` fixture that never ran
// through a real boot script.
//
// The default (no `include-compiler`) release: `run-entry` — the
// always-available, no-compiler dispatch path (ADR 0125 §1.5/§1.7), also
// what `bin/<name> eval`/`rpc` use — reaches a real project class, and
// `eval` (source) is refused with `release_mode_no_compiler`.
//
// `run_test_file_opts` skips `clear_bindings` for this file, matching
// `release_console_default.btscript` — see its own doc for why
// (`Session current clear` is itself an eval, always refused here).

:run-entry ReleaseSmoke ping
// => 42

1 + 1
// => ERROR: OTP release
